Let $S$ be the subset of indices of the foods chosen.
Let $V_i, A_i, C_i$ be the vitamin type, vitamin amount, and calorie count for the $i$-th food.
The total calories consumed is $\sum_{i \in S} C_i$.
The amount of vitamin $v$ consumed is $\sum_{i \in S, V_i = v} A_i$.
We want to maximize $\min(\text{vit}_1, \text{vit}_2, \text{vit}_3)$ subject to $\sum_{i \in S} C_i \le X$.

